<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38358" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Priscus</span></b> , i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman surname</i>,
				<i>the elder.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of <i>the
				first Tarquin</i>: Priscus Tarquinius est dictus, quia prius
			fuit quam Superbus Tarquinius, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				226</span></i> Müll.; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
			34</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Tarquinius Numicius Priscus, <i><span class="en">Liv. 2,
			63</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			Helvidius Priscus, <i><span class="en">Suet. Vesp.
			15</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			Two Latin poets: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Priscus uterque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 4, 16, 10</span></i>
			 Burm. ad loc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
